## Original Content
L’entrée dans la course à l’Élysée de Raphaël Glucksmann dans le cadre de la primaire socialiste, peut-être bientôt suivie par celles d’Olivier Faure et de Boris Vallaud, et par la candidature hors primaire du communiste Fabien Roussel illustrent la difficulté de s’y retrouver face à la pléthore de candidatures à gauche. France 24 fait le point.

## Summary
The article discusses the entry of multiple candidates on the left into the French presidential election, highlighting Raphaël Glucksmann's participation in the socialist primary and potential candidacies of Olivier Faure and Boris Vallaud. It also notes Fabien Roussel's candidacy as a communist outside the primary, illustrating the challenges of a crowded field.

## Key Points
- Raphaël Glucksmann has entered the socialist primary for the French presidential election.
- Olivier Faure and Boris Vallaud may also join the primary.
- Fabien Roussel is running as a communist candidate outside the primary.
- The multitude of candidacies on the left complicates political consolidation and strategy.


